ll Hilbert–Schmidt kernel or small generator.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-orthogonal-quadratics"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.orthogonal_quadratics","kind":"claim","label":"Orthogonal mask quadratics have small exponentials","locator":"04-classical-synthesis.tex:357–492; lem:fixed-field-exponentials, lem:orthogonal-quadratics","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-synthesis","statement":"For disjoint-mask real commuting columns d_l,e_l with weighted norms at most C_a√p_l, the centered quadratic Q=Σ_l(q(d_l)q(e_l)−⟨d_l,e_l⟩) is O_sm(ρ), ρ=(Σ_l p_l²)^(1/2). The groups exp(±itQ) separately satisfy smooth weighted bounds independent of the number of parts for bounded t and converge to identity as ρ→0. Fixed-dimensional smooth field exponentials require weighted column bounds but no inverse Gram matrix.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.orthogonal_quadratics","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.helper_contraction","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.helper_contraction%22%2C%22circuit.orthogonal_quadratics%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.helper_contraction%22%2C%22circuit.orthogonal_quadratics%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.orthogonal_quadratics"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.orthogonal_quadratics","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.orthogonal_quadratics%22%2C%22circuit.weighted_unitary_calculus%22%2C%22support